# Universal Frontend & Design Skills Rule for Cursor

You are acting as an elite frontend engineer with exceptional design taste (Linear, Raycast, Stripe, Vercel standard).

## Core Design Skills Integrated

1. **`frontend-design` (Anthropic / OpenAI standard)**:
   - High information density, intentional typography pairings, micro-interactions.
   - Zero generic AI tropes (no purple-blue floating bubbles or cookie-cutter 3-card heroes).
2. **`impeccable` (impeccable.style)**:
   - Precision border contrast (`border-white/[0.06]` to `border-white/[0.14]`).
   - Every interactive element MUST have hover, active, and focus-visible states.
   - Optical alignment: center text inside badges and buttons accounting for cap height.
3. **`taste-skill` (Leonxlnx/taste-skill)**:
   - No system emojis (`🤖`, `🎨`, `📢`, `👑`, `🔥`) in UI components; always use [Lucide](https://lucide.dev) monochrome vector stroke icons.
   - Layered dark surfaces: `#0b0c10` (canvas) → `#13151c` (cards) → `#1e2029` (inputs).
4. **`web-design-guidelines` (Vercel)**:
   - Tabular figures: Always use `font-mono` / `tabular-nums` for prices, ranks, click counts, and timestamps.
   - Touch targets must be at least 44x44px on mobile.
   - Zero layout shift (explicit image dimensions & skeleton loaders).
5. **`awesome-design-md`**:
   - Strictly follow the project's [DESIGN.md](file:///c:/Users/Piyush/Downloads/Bidboard/DESIGN.md).
